# Chefaa Medications Extraction: Consolidated Dataset and Rate-Limited Scaling Strategy (Batch 1)

## Executive Summary

This report documents the creation of a consolidated dataset for Chefaa medication product pages and sets out a practical, rate-limit-aware strategy to scale toward the target of 200 medications within Batch 1. The work concentrated on two fronts: first, deduplicating and structuring the initial medication dataset; second, expanding coverage by systematically tapping additional category listing pages to secure more product URLs, while applying disciplined cooldown tactics to mitigate rate limiting.

An initial seed set of 28 product URLs, harvested from two listing files, yielded approximately 12 successfully extracted products with varying levels of completeness. Expansion via a previously untapped listing file (page 124) immediately surfaced 20 new product candidates, demonstrating that a structured crawl of category pages can unlock meaningful incremental coverage. To sustain throughput, the strategy prioritizes staggered processing windows, jittered delays between requests, and a strict health monitoring regimen.

Pricing fields exhibit mixed precision across products. Where prices are available, they are captured in Egyptian Pounds (EGP) with near-real-time delivery windows commonly stated as 30–60 minutes. However, the dataset currently lacks a single, harmonized approach to price normalization, a gap addressed later in the standardization plan.

The immediate next phase focuses on: (1) finalizing the consolidation of the initial 12 products, (2) expanding extraction through listing files beyond page 124, and (3) enforcing a cooldown protocol with health monitoring. The operational objective for the next cycle is to reach at least 50 unique medications, with complete bilingual coverage where source pages allow, and to document all access policies and constraints for reproducibility and governance.

To frame the current state and immediate next steps, the following table summarizes the key metrics.

