## Consolidation Plan and Deduplication Strategy

The consolidation will merge the initial medications array and the new_extracted_medications array into a single medications list under a unified schema. Deduplication will be performed on product_url as the canonical key, ensuring each product appears once.

Field normalization will be applied to bilingual pairs, active ingredients, therapeutic indications, dosage, contraindications and warnings, side effects and precautions, storage conditions, clinical information, and pricing. Where a field is missing, it will be explicitly set to null rather than left undefined, preserving traceability and enabling later enrichment.

To support field-level QA, the following table maps required fields to source locations and completeness status.

Table 4. Field-to-source mapping and completeness checklist

| Field | Source Location | Status | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| product_id | Product page / Listing file | Partial | Populate from listing where possible; validate against page slug |
| product_name_arabic | Product page | Partial | Prefer product page; fallback to listing name |
| product_name_english | Product page | Partial | Prefer product page; fallback to listing name |
| product_url | Listing file | Complete | Canonical deduplication key |
| description.arabic | Product page | Partial | Varies by product; use fallback where missing |
| description.english | Product page | Partial | Varies by product; use fallback where missing |
| specifications.form | Product page | Partial | Standardize enums (tablet, drops, syrup, etc.) |
| specifications.strength/pack_size | Product page | Partial | Normalize units and format |
| active_ingredients | Product page | Partial | Extract name, concentration, unit; infer only when explicit |
| therapeutic_indications | Product page | Partial | Prefer bilingual lists; consolidate duplicates |
| dosage_and_administration | Product page | Partial | Capture age groups and dosing; null if absent |
| contraindications_and_warnings | Product page | Partial | Preserve explicit items; null if absent |
| side_effects_and_precautions | Product page | Partial | Capture explicit items; null if absent |
| storage_conditions | Product page | Partial | Normalize storage statements; null if absent |
| clinical_information | Product page | Partial | Keep concise mechanism notes; null if absent |
| pricing.price_egp | Product page / Listing | Partial | Harmonize numeric format and currency |
| pricing.currency | Product page / Listing | Partial | Default to EGP when implied |
| pricing.availability_status | Product page / Listing | Partial | Standardize status labels |
| prescription_required | Product page | Partial | Normalize to boolean; default false when unknown |

The consolidation will be governed by a QA checklist covering normalization rules, null handling, and JSON schema validation. Any schema regressions will be flagged and corrected before merging.

## Extraction Progress and Completeness Assessment

Initial consolidation suggests approximately 12 successfully extracted products from the 28-URL seed set, with notable variation in content richness across fields. Several extractions are partial: pages may omit key sections such as dosage, contraindications, side effects, storage conditions, or even explicit active ingredient lists. Pricing is generally present but inconsistently formatted.

Examples highlight both breadth and gaps:

- Plavix illustrates detailed indications and dosing guidance and includes specific warnings such as grapefruit avoidance.[^2]
- Plendil provides a thorough mechanism of action and clear indications, yet lists no contraindications or side effects.[^3]
- Zyrtec drops offer comprehensive pediatric dosing, administration guidance, and mechanism of action, with explicit dosing tiers by age.[^18]
- Prontogest provides a detailed description, indications, and dosage recommendations.[^13]

